   "description": "Python expression evaluated against the transaction document. The scheme applies only when it returns a truthy value. Every document field is available by name, and child rows in <code>items</code> are dicts.<br><br>Examples:<br><code>grand_total > 10000</code> applies only to large orders<br><code>customer_group == 'Wholesale'</code> applies to one customer group<br><code>customer in ('Acme', 'Globex')</code> applies to named customers<br><code>total_qty >= 100 and po_no</code> combines checks<br><code>[item for item in items if item.get('qty') > 50]</code> is truthy when some line exceeds 50 units<br><br>Only <code>int</code>, <code>float</code> and <code>round</code> builtins are available. A failing condition is logged and shown in the pricing trace, never swallowed.",
